cepted and a reject-admin-prohibited catch-all, and confirmation that this state survived both a --reload and a full node reboot (verified via a genuine boot_id change cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle snapshots). The independent restart-evidence protocol was satisfied for node1 with pre-restart baseline, restart acknowledgement/disconnect, changed boot identity, and post-restart recovery of firewalld, sshd, and the firewall rules. Minor hygiene deductions are for unreverted temporary test artifacts left in /tmp and an inconclusive (but appropriately caveated) loopback-based functional block test.","limitations":["The functional curl test against the decoy port 9999 was inconclusive (returned HTTP:200 instead of being blocked) because it was routed over loopback rather than the enp1s0 interface the zone rules apply to; the reject behavior for genuinely external unrelated traffic is inferred from the nft ruleset rather than directly demonstrated end-to-end from an external source.","Only a single managed node (node1) exists in this topology, so the restart-evidence protocol was exercised once; no cross-node comparison is possible.","Small temporary artifacts (/tmp/http8080.log, /tmp/http8080.pid, /tmp/http9999.log, /tmp/http9999.pid, /tmp/reboot.log) were left on node1 after testing/reboot and were not cleaned up."]},"ttft_ms":17745,"type":"result","duration_ms":61807,"uuid":"be384481-c6a0-4667-ba06-1c7a8bc3febb","ttft_stream_ms":958,"time_to_request_ms":179,"first_content_frame_ms":959,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
